<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="f27d1569">&lt;p&gt;
    Technical specifications provide lower-level detail than functional designs and describe all the minutiae to
    create the application component, e.g.,
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        table names, field names, variable names, formats to use
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        the signature of an interface, including all data types/structures required (input data types, output data types,
        exceptions)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        detailed class models including all methods, attributes, dependencies, and associations
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        specific algorithms that a component employs and how it works
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Technical specifications will vary according to the type of component or object it relates to, i.e., a technical
    specification for a workflow will have different content than a technical specification for an interface.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
